  "concreteRepairs": [
    "The inherited nine-step 2.52m near flight from y=.067, 1.52m foot landing and broad causeway are retired. Four actual closed .175m/.28m steps rise from the lantern island at y=.62 over 1.12m, with a .66m landing and short guards joined to the bridge. The near bridge endpoint and lantern anchor are unchanged.",
    "A narrow .96m forecourt branch and 1.10m rear branch contain twelve actual closed worn flagstones. Refined top boundary vertices are shared exactly with new sides/bottoms; the older coarse-rim T-junction preflight is preserved. Real crowns, hollows, pits and chipped outlines remain geometry.",
    "Seven low inherited tower-walk slabs crossing the lantern/stair plan are retired. Their old terrain reservation is limited to surviving slabs at z<-7.65. The rear branch meets the actual front of surviving slab index7 at z=-7.71 with a 10mm lap.",
    "The actual connected lantern soil field now reaches y=.58 beneath the fixed .70m support and .77m lantern anchor, instead of R06 triangle y=-.025. Its shore has a smaller eroded outline. A real mineral toe and existing support stone are partly embedded, not separate hovering support feet.",
    "The hall terrace retains its cap, short bearings and nine embedded gallery brackets. Its 129 ruler-straight face stones are replaced by81 closed irregular ashlar with changing joint heights/depth and actual per-vertex block tone. The real hall-side soil/mineral shoulder embeds lower courses.",
    "R08 oversized pale mineral exposures were rendered and rejected. R09 uses seven lower deep-seated wet-dark hall bank pieces and one filtered lantern mineral toe, from original CC0 scan buffers with positive uniform transforms. They are independent of structural pier support.",
    "Eleven garden broadleaf/blossom rigid poses were recovered from the actual frozen R06 CPU geometry/RNG recipe and added to the existing56 held forest records, preventing lower-plant acceptance from rotating those good trees. The recovery uses original rock position/index/normal ray buffers and botanical primitive counts, with no browser, image, GPU or mesh export."
  ],
